==================================================================
 Part 1: overflow versus saturation (4x4 array, INT8, 16-bit accumulators)
==================================================================
  Every input is -128 and K = 8, so each output is 8 x 16,384 = 131072
  True answer (no limit)               131072
  Hardware, wrapping accumulators           0   (as expected)
  Hardware, saturating accumulators     32767   (as expected)
  Wrapping turns 131,072 into 0. Saturating stops at the largest 16-bit value:
  still wrong, but by the least possible amount, and the sign never flips.

  Random 32x32 times 32x32: 327 of 1024 true answers do not fit in 16 bits.
    wrapping:   327 wrong, worst error 131072
    saturating: 468 wrong, worst error 70704
  Saturation also broke 141 results whose final value fits in 16 bits: a partial
  sum overflowed on the way and was clamped. Wrapping gets those right because the
  overflows cancel out. So saturation bounds the error but depends on the order.
  PASS  wrapping hardware matches its model (1024/1024)
  PASS  saturating hardware matches its model (1024/1024)

==================================================================
 Part 2: post-processing unit (bias + requantize + ReLU)
   y = clamp( round( (acc + bias) x 16384 / 2^22 ), lo, 127 )   scale = 1/256
==================================================================
  PASS  ReLU on : 400/400 outputs correct
  PASS  ReLU off: 400/400 outputs correct

        acc + bias   exact value   ReLU off   ReLU on
                 0          0.00          0         0
               128          0.50          1         1
               384          1.50          2         2
              -128         -0.50          0         0
              -384         -1.50         -1         0
        1073741824    4194304.00        127       127
       -1073741824   -4194304.00       -128         0
               255          1.00          1         1
              4632         18.09         18        18
            -30330       -118.48       -118         0
  Halves round up (0.5 -> 1, -0.5 -> 0). Results outside -128..127 are clamped,
  and ReLU sets negatives to 0. One result per clock; 3 pipeline stages.

